Z||000008||dman||07-05-2000||02:23 PM||||Hi RobertVol. VSS is the Vehicle Speed Sensor. I had an old parts car that had its VSS disconnected. Actually the wiring to it was broken off. I had a VSS error as well, code 24 I think. If your ECM is not getting a speed signal then you'll get that code. Surprisingly when I reconnected my VSS, my speedometer started working again, but I still had the VSS code!<P>The VSS signal goes first to your speedometer, your speedo then divides the signal in half before sending it to your ECM. If there is a problem anywhere along the line then you'll get that VSS signal.<P>BTW, on another fiero I had my speedo stopped working and the car ran like crap. It turns out I forgotten that I had pulled a fuse out (to swap into another fiero I had). This fuse powered my speedo, and I guess my ECM was no longer getting a signal.<P>I don't know why your car is getting the code 24, and whether or not it was related to your tach filter, but now you have some more info about the VSS.||||reg||1
Z||000009||JohnnyK||07-05-2000||03:23 PM||||All I did was go to a junkyard and rip one off of a car.. Didn't look too nice, but it worked, and it was free.||||reg||1
Z||000010||RobertVol||07-05-2000||03:24 PM||||Thanks for the info, appreciate it !<P>This is probably just timing but my car has slacked off on performance ever since I got the code and the tach starting going funny.<P>But it may not be related since it seems when things do go wrong with my cars they seem to happen in two's. And on acceleration I am starting to hear a rattling sound from the back hmmmm Its only at 55k miles but after 13 yrs its probably something with the exaust area. Its just same timing i guess Tach starts jumping car starts running rough! Yeah it probably is  that dreaded exaust issue. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||07-05-2000||11:27 PM||||disconnect the tack filter. the car will perfectly run w/o it.<P>then clear the ECM and see if the VSS error goes away. If the VSS error comes back it's a seperate problem that must be fixed. The car will never run right without a VSS feed to the ECM.||||reg||1
